  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Humid with additional showers/thunderstorms \npossible late today through the first half of tonight along and \nahead of a cold front moving south from New York state. \n\nA weak ridge of high pressure over Central PA this morning will\nmove east and off the New Jersey coast this afternoon allowing\nwarm, humid air to push northeast across the state this afternoon\nand evening. Much of today will be partly to mostly sunny (SE\nhalf of the CWA) and mostly cloudy (NW) but generally dry, with\na light NW breeze across the eastern half of the state, and a \nlight southwesterly breeze over the west - freshening to around \n10 kts this afternoon. \n\nThis warmer and more moist air streaming NE above the shallow\nand slightly cooler airmass over the Northern half of the state\nwill lead to variable amounts stratus and stratocu this \nmorning, but vertical mixing will lift cloud bases by 14-17Z \nKUNV, KAOO and KJST. \n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms will be possible this \nevening until shortly after midnight, along and just ahead of a \ncold front that will be drifting south from New York State and a\nmid and upper level WNW jet max approaching from the Glakes \nregion. HREF's MU CAPE rising to between 1000-1500 J/KG will \ncreate the opportunity for moderately strong updrafts and the \npotential for some isolated wind damage from peak gusts of 40-45\nkts and small hail.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Seasonably cooler and less humid Friday and\nSaturday \n\nComfortably cooler and noticeably drier (less humid) air \naccompanies seasonably strong/Canadian high pressure building \nsoutheast from the Upper Midwest Friday night through Saturday.  \n\nBelow normal pwats will facilitate pleasant days and crisp\nnights (40s and 50s most locations Friday night/AM Saturday).",
